identical tome existed on a dimension ruled by Oranbegans who were not remotely peace-loving. You battled the evil Oranbegans, retrieved the tome, and still found time to contemplate the infinite variety of the multiverse. <br><br>You took the tome to Azuria, who had agreed to perform the ritual. <br><br>Then you found yourself facing a disaster: a rupture had opened at the Walldorf Factory in Paragon City! Dozens of powerful psychic Clockwork had spilled from the rupture onto the streets of your hometown! You battled back the Clockwork and closed the rupture, but your job wasn't over. <br><br>A rupture at the Jamison Office Park brought a bevy of malevolent ghosts to your city. Once again, you skunked the villains and put an end to the dimensional rupture. <br><br>While Azuria reunited the scientists' disparate halves, you went to speak to Tina Macintyre. She theorized that the force that ripped apart the scientists' dimensional fabric could do the same thing to an entire world. If you couldn't stop the dimensional ruptures, Paragon City might soon be strewn across the multiverse. <br><br>Reunited with their other halves, the scientists found they could speak normally once more. They told you that, before they were lost, they had learned that someone might be deliberately causing the ruptures. You set out into the multiverse to take readings from dimensional ruptures so Portal Corporation could evaluate this new theory. <br><br>The technicians analyzed your data and came to the conclusion that the ruptures had originated from dimension Lamda Rho 57-20, better known as Werewolf World. You went to seek out the master of Werewolf World, Requiem, but he eluded you. He did, however, briefly touch your mind. You were more convinced than ever that he was responsible for the ruptures. <br><br>You needed a way to force Requiem to show himself. You consulted Peter Stemitz, who had a bright idea. If you could find a sample of pure flame, you might be able to draw Requiem into the light. Azuria gave you a candle, and Maria Jenkins drew forth the pure flame. <br><br>You took the flame to Werewolf World and, as predicted, Requiem was drawn to it. However, time was running short, and you escaped from Werewolf World just before the entire dimension was torn from the fabric of the multiverse. It seemed that Requiem's dimensional tampering had caught up with him. And yet you had to wonder: how had Requiem caused all this chaos? Perhaps he had powers you had never imagined. Or perhaps there was someone else in the shadows, who had not yet been brought into light."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P890181051" "Something's happened, {HeroName}, something bad. A group of Portal Corporation scientists set up a observation post in the dimension of the Hydra Men. Their plan was to stay out of sight and collect data, but something seems to have gone wrong. I can't contact the team at all! <A HREF={ACCEPT}>I need you to go in there and find those scientists, {HeroName}.</A> Don't come back without them."
// AcceptString :
"P1818120884" "Find the missing scientists"
// SendOffString :
"P4060818310" "Contact was perfect until just this morning, but suddenly the team's signal went all wonky. I really don't know what to expect."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2525337753" "Seek the missing scientists"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2730174886" "We still don't know where Portal Corp's scientists are!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3858807769" "You wish Portal Corporation would keep better track of their scientists."
// Script Variable PATROLLER1_SEARCHING_DIALOG :
"P856364347" ""
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P707705343" "O'ai''e"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Rubble 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ModelDisplayName :
"P1511201128" "Pile of rubble"
// Description :
"P3360217240" "Clues to find"
// SingularDescription :
"P883117697" "Find the last clue!"
// InteractBeginString :
"P1977069074" "You begin to sift through the rubble."
// InteractInterruptedString :
"P2557807414" "You have been interrupted!"
// InteractCompleteString :
"P2502690835" "You have finished searching the rubble."
// InteractActionString :
"P4018751421" "Sifting..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1697731175" "You found a notebook!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Ruptures 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ModelDisplayName :
"P3794478536" "Dimensional rupture"
// InteractBeginString :
"P1324195320" "You begin to examine the dimensional rupture."
// InteractCompleteString :
"P2390100836" "You have finished examining the rupture."
// InteractActionString :
"P1412195360" "Examining..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2078155183" "You can't tell much about this rupture, but you're alarmed by its presence."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2562028981" "You found only one trace of the missing scientists: their research notes."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3466320012" "No scientists, huh? But a dimensional rupture the size of a Volkswagen. Well, {HeroName}, I think you know what I'm about to tell you. Portal Corporation's scientists are lost somewhere within the multiverse. Lucky I've got you to help me find them."
// RandomFameString :
"P265151428" "{HeroName}'s looking for some missing scientists."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3763957939" "Portal Corporation's scientists are lost somewhere in the multiverse, and we need to find them quickly. Unfortunately, looking for a group of people in the multiverse is a bit like looking for a needle in a haystack. Actually, it's nowhere near that easy. That's why I've asked Dr. Tina Macintyre to help us out. Go see if she can cook up anything to speed this search along.</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P2052818333" "Go see Tina Macintyre"
// SendOffString :
"P3440860585" "Tina knows what it's like to lose her comrades. I can assure you, no one is more dedicated to this mission than she."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound2_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P4017860087" "Talk to Tina Macintyre"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2871321607" "I think Tina can help us find those missing scientists."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4067116939" "Unai spoke to me about the missing scientists, and I think I've developed something to help you find them. I'm calling it a dimensional triangulator. You'll have to visit several dimensions to get enough data, but it should help me pinpoint the dimension our wayward scientists have landed on. While you're searching, keep an eye out for dimensional ruptures. They've been giving us a lot of trouble lately."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound2_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3734784362" "Get data from 1st dimension"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3538030988" "That dimensional triangulator won't do us any good in this world, {HeroName}. You've got to take it for a spin."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P110059655" "In this world, or in any other, the Freaks' choice of music is always solid metal."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Ruptures 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P3573925640" "ruptures to catalog"
// SingularDescription :
"P3413167287" "Catalog the last rupture!"
// InteractBeginString :
"P1776760865" "You begin examining the rupture."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2141339582" "You make a note of the rupture's location."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3049440291" "You have collected enough data from this dimension."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound2_Part3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1573799913" "Get data from 2nd dimension"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3167529636" "We need more data if we're going to find those missing scientists."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P4111297835" "According to Tina Macintyre, this dimension's Knives of Artemis are firmly in control. You only hope they're not as brutal as the Knives of your own world."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Ruptures2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound2_Part4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P4018333608" "Get data from last dimension"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1723492233" "One more dimension to go, {HeroName}. A little more data, and we'll have the location of our missing scientists."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3470833674" "Tina Macintyre couldn't tell you who you'd face in this unexplored dimension."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Ruptures3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2890460959" "I have to admire your gumption, {HeroName}. You stuck it out through three brutal dimensions, just to get us the data we need. I'll get the techs to work on this; with any luck, we'll soon have the location of the missing scientists. You say you found a total of 21 dimensional ruptures on your travels? They'll want to know about that, I'm sure. These ruptures are getting out of hand!"
// RandomFameString :
"P794852270" "Portal Corporation sure is keeping {HeroName} busy!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1327677719" "Ok, {HeroName}, Portal Corporation analyzed all the data you brought us. It was a little sketchy, but we think we've narrowed down the location of our missing scientists. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>Now all you need to do is extract them.</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P3213804735" "Extract the missing scientists"
// SendOffString :
"P153460566" "I have to warn you, the world we're sending you to is inhabited exclusively by the Devouring Earth. Chances are they'll make your job a little harder."
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2306925576" "We need Portal Corp's scientists back safe and sound."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3659787976" "This lush landscape would truly seem like a paradise, were it not for the nearby presence of the Devouring Earth."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Hostage1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ModelDisplayName :
"P725058278" "Portal Corporation scientist"
// Description :
"P4245099803" "scientists to save"
// SingularDescription :
"P159809516" "Save the last scientist!"
// InteractCompleteString :
"P3977190599" "Boats on banana paper."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Hostage2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// InteractCompleteString :
"P1282828390" "Pink snowflakes write sculpture."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Hostage3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// InteractCompleteString :
"P3356175454" "You sing happiness go home?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Hostage4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// InteractCompleteString :
"P4231124995" "Crustacean fancy pants plaza."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Hostage5 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// InteractCompleteString :
"P2415883797" "Peaches! Sourdough! Agate! Marine!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Hostage6 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// InteractCompleteString :
"P831463773" "Zip zop."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1632770636" "You rescued the Portal Corporation scientists."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P121703801" "Thanks for getting those scientists back for us, {HeroName}. I only wish they were in better condition. I haven't been able to get a single straight answer out of them, they just keep saying things like, 'The carrot ate my socks.' Something has addled their brains, and we need to find out what."
// RandomFameString :
"P1796045006" "{HeroName} saved some Portal Corporation scientists!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Errand4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1502317707" "Portal Corporation is extremely grateful to you for rescuing those scientists. I just wish we knew what was wrong with them! They're still speaking nothing but gibberish! We sent them over to Dr. Steven Sheridan for a quick check up. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>Will you go collect the results?</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P1224324954" "Collect the results of Dr. Sheridan's examination"
// SendOffString :
"P3822603920" "Sheridan's the best doc I know. Maybe he can get to the bottom of this."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3274094945" "Talk to Dr. Steven Sheridan"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2415840517" "I need to know what Sheridan has to say about those addled Portal Corporation scientists."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2000643470" "I've examined the Portal Corporation scientists, and even I was amazed at my findings. {HeroName}, I believe that you actually only saved half the scientists. Not half their number; half of each person! Allow me to explain. <br><br>When you first went looking for the scientists, you found only a dimensional rupture. Well, it's my belief that this rupture actually fractured the scientists, splitting them into two people. One half got sent to the Devouring Earth's world. And the other half? Still lost somewhere within the multiverse. Perhaps the rest of Portal's brain trust can help you figure out where."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3479632490" "So, each scientist you saved is actually just half of the original person? Well, if Sheridan says so. I guess we'll need to locate the other halves, then see if we can find a way to unite them."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission5 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3372585746" "So, Steven Sheridan thinks the Portal scientists were torn in two, and one half is still out there, somewhere in the multiverse. I guess that explains the sketchy data we got the last time you tried to pinpoint their location. I had the techs check out that data again, and they think they've figured out the location of the scientists' other halves. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>Will you go rescue them?</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P214630277" "Rescue the scientists' other halves"
// SendOffString :
"P796010728" "You'll be heading for a dimension packed with Nemesis soldiers. Watch your back."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3942580554" "Rescue scientists' other halves"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P451955600" "Half a scientist isn't much good to Portal Corporation. We need the full deal."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P19791765" "Portal Corporation has charted many dimensions ruled by one version of Nemesis or another. They are rich and varied, but all equally deadly."
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2390152767" "What do you make of these unusual strangers?"
// Script Variable ACTOR2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2589404395" "They are insane. Nemesis will probably want them eliminated."
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P4013339183" "You trespass upon Nemesis' land!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Hostage1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// InteractCompleteString :
"P1889586396" "Orange juice? Canasta!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Hostage2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// InteractCompleteString :
"P1436273543" "Only the lonely fish for currents."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Hostage3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// InteractCompleteString :
"P4291520056" "We clash in time for tea."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Hostage4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// InteractCompleteString :
"P3964663313" "Shell nozzle fruity tree."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Hostage5 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// InteractCompleteString :
"P2509703672" "Hero? Joy is punk Rolex."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Hostage6 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// InteractCompleteString :
"P2750588830" "Clip clop."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1091056362" "You rescued the scientists' other halves"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2455555342" "Good work, {HeroName}. You rescued the scientists' other halves. Now all we have to do is figure out how to rejoin them. I'm not good at this whole dimensional fabric mumbo jumbo. This may take some doing."
// RandomFameString :
"P2616492665" "The paper says {HeroName} just saved some Portal Corporation scientists. Talk about deja vu."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound6 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3839171294" "You know, I have to admit I sort of hoped that once you had rescued both halves of the Portal Corporation scientists, they would just snap back together. You know, their dimensional fabric would just knit itself right up. But I guess that's not the way it works; each scientist is still in two pieces. And still spouting nothing but nonsense. The technicians are stumped, and I think we may need to give science a rest and try a magical solution. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>Will you go speak to Azuria about reuniting the scientists' disparate halves?</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P2875850414" "Speak to Azuria about reuniting the scientists' disparate halves"
// SendOffString :
"P2209721253" "This is new ground we're treading on, {HeroName}. I really hope Azuria can help."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound6_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P4048120735" "Talk to Azuria"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P204739194" "I need to know if Azuria can help us."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2621113769" "I would like to help you, {HeroName}, but this is uncharted territory. I suspect that no one on this world knows of a spell that can reunite a person torn apart by a dimensional rupture. I do have an idea, though. I once heard that Portal Corporation had located a dimension filled with peaceful Oranbegans, a pacifist society that never turned into the bloodthirsty Circle of Thorns. Perhaps you can seek them out? Their society was based entirely on magic; I imagine their lore is millennia beyond our own."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound6_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2912318583" "Defeat all villains in area"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2327771927" "Azuria sent you to the Oranbegans for help. I'm sure she knows what she's doing."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2157300056" "A screech rips through the air. It seems the Oranbegans are under attack!"
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2360704844" "What has brought us here?"
// Script Variable ACTOR2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3005515118" "These mages are doubtless to blame! Kill them!"
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P2026582743" "We will feast upon you!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - cot1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ModelDisplayName :
"P374315029" "Oranbegan"
// Description :
"P253891913" "mages to save"
// SingularDescription :
"P3677100291" "Save last mage!"
// InteractCompleteString :
"P775866755" "I believe I can help you."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1059772649" "You got the {ITEM_NAME}!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - cot2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// InteractCompleteString :
"P4144249952" "They are animals!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - cot3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// InteractCompleteString :
"P648407216" "This is exactly why we outlaw all violence!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - cot4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// InteractCompleteString :
"P3687764896" "They came from a dimensional rupture!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Ruptures 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P3931324677" "ruptures to close"
// SingularDescription :
"P1220398124" "Close last rupture!"
// InteractBeginString :
"P1928151685" "You begin to close the rupture."
// InteractCompleteString :
"P2442332334" "You have finished closing the rupture."
// InteractActionString :
"P4200538943" "Closing rupture..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4050578253" "You rescued the mages from the Banished Pantheon!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2087082554" "Good work, {HeroName}! If this Oranbegan ritual works, we'll have our scientists back, good as new! Of course, I don't think that means we can rest on our laurels. I'm pretty worried about these dimensional ruptures; everything we've heard indicates that they're becoming a huge problem. Not just for us, but for other dimensions. If that's true, {HeroName}, then the fate of the entire multiverse may well rest on your shoulders. Not too much pressure, eh?"
// RandomFameString :
"P2054715809" "Lately, {HeroName}'s been spending more time out of our dimension than in it!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission7 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3511822723" "According to those Circle of Thorns mages you rescued, we need to get our hands on the Tome of Persephone before we  can perform this ritual. Only problem is, the Tome of Persephone was destroyed long, long ago, back when Nero was emperor of Rome. I've located a dimension that has an existing copy of the tome. Unfortunately, it's a dimension full of Circle mages, and they aren't nearly as friendly as the last ones. The tome's sure to be well-guarded, but we've got to have it. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>Will you recover the Tome of Persephone?</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P2394767667" "Recover the Tome of Persephone"
// SendOffString :
"P4014642387" "Persephone lived her life half in sunlight, half in shadow. Her tome contains many rituals dealing with the union of two disparate objects or beings."
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3753310540" "We need that tome, {HeroName}."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P1545055133" "These caves have been furnished with lavish gold candlesticks and lovely marble sculptures."
// Script Variable PATROLLER1_SEARCHING_DIALOG :
"P1190304474" "An alien presence has invaded Oranbega!"
// Script Variable PATROLLER_ATTACK_DIALOG1 :
"P851806726" "Destroy the trespasser!"
// Script Variable PATROLLER_ATTACK_DIALOG2 :
"P2728861151" "You will never leave our halls!"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P755958052" "Aceotes"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P4040423238" "Who would invade my domain?"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P3940874676" "You shall not take my treasures!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Correct 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ModelDisplayName :
"P3472277936" "Treasure chest"
// Description :
"P4121069735" "Find the tome!"
// InteractBeginString :
"P3387836727" "You begin to open the chest."
// InteractCompleteString :
"P675679111" "The chest is open."
// InteractActionString :
"P1143515829" "Opening..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Wrong 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1273649207" "You found a bejeweled crown. Interesting, but not what you're looking for."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Sorry 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4138847586" "You found several moldy clay jars. Interesting, but not what you're looking for."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - NotThisChest 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3686276580" "You found an ancient spear. Interesting, but not what you're looking for."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - UnUh 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P719984588" "You found an emerald necklace. Interesting, but not what you're looking for."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - TryAgain 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1581328794" "You found a massive conch shell. Interesting, but not what you're looking for."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Incorrectamundo 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2183935037" "You found a crystal goblet. Interesting, but not what you're looking for."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2421208539" "You found the Tome of Persephone!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1503062160" "Great work. That tome is the last thing we need to perform the spell that will help those altered Portal scientists. I must say, it's remarkable how varied the multiverse is. On one dimension, the Oranbegans are as peaceful as can be. On another, they'll tear your head off at a moment's notice!"
// RandomFameString :
"P4007149232" "According to {HeroName}, it's a rich and varied multiverse!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Errand8 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3212698256" "Azuria's agreed to perform the ritual that will reunite the sundered Portal scientists. All she needs is that Tome of Persephone; then she can get to work. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>Will you take the tome to her?</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P1487540928" "Take the tome to Azuria"
// SendOffString :
"P2939525990" "If Azuria can't help those scientists, no one can."
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P539915883" "Azuria needs that tome!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3737797717" "Thank you, {HeroName}. If the information provided by the Oranbegans was correct, I should be able to perform the ritual to reunite the sundered halves of those poor scientists. It will take some time. <br><br>I must warn you of something. I have sensed a presence reaching out from the Aether. A most malevolent presence. It may be that a conscious mind is behind these dreadful dimensional ruptures. If that's so, I fear you must be the one to face it down."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3915321798" "Well, the tome is in good hands now: Azuria's. If anyone can help those scientists, it's her. I'll keep looking into these dimensional ruptures. Something tells me we're not done with them yet."
// RandomFameString :
"P3478592237" "I saw {HeroName} running around carrying some moldy old book."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission9 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1638553608" "You did good work helping those Portal scientists, {HeroName}. But it looks as if the mages you rescued are correct: the number of dimensional ruptures is increasing exponentially! A rupture opened just minutes ago right here in Paragon City! We need to close it, but, more importantly, we need to get rid of the creatures that came through. I've got reports of psychic Clockwork in the old Walldorf Factory. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>I need you to stop those Clockwork and close that rupture!</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P1802072262" "Stop the villains and close the ruptures"
// SendOffString :
"P2169068256" "This is bad, {HeroName}. We need to deal with these ruptures before all the dangers of the multiverse wind up in our back yard!"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1123338" "Defeat all Clockwork at factory"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3383708670" "Those otherworldly Clockwork are a real menace!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// LocationName :
"P1352680398" "Walldorf Factory"
// EntryString :
"P4256017253" "The Clockwork King's world is one of Portal Corporation's restricted dimensions. It's terrifying to think that his creations are in Paragon City!"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P977814434" "Cannon Prince"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Ruptures 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P2928345632" "Close the rupture!"
// InteractBeginString :
"P1217385078" "You begin to close the dimensional rupture."
// InteractCompleteString :
"P2701545640" "You have closed the dimensional rupture."
// InteractActionString :
"P19986288" "Closing..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskBegin 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2284046631" "Here's a dimensional stabilizer. Portal Corporation has been working round the clock to improve this little baby, and they think they've succeeded."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4220618681" "You defeated the Clockwork and closed the dimensional rupture."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1300125573" "Whew, {HeroName}, I owe you for that one. You did a good, clean job, and you did it fast. If these ruptures keep opening, I'm going to have to start calling in all my favors from the hero community. We simply can't let another dimension's villains get a foothold in Paragon City! It can't happen!"
// RandomFameString :
"P1476118138" "Did you see those crazy Clockwork over at the Walldorf Factory? I never knew Clockwork could get that strong!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission10 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2689681783" "Portal is still working around the clock to stay on top of the rupture situation. I've got another rupture open at the Jamison Office Park, and I need you to take care of it. We got a force field up quickly, but there are still a lot of people trapped inside. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>Get over to Jamison, stop the villains, and close the rupture!</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P3773525939" "Defeat the villains and close the rupture"
// SendOffString :
"P2860022892" "According to reports, that office park is full of some sort of malevolent ghosts!"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2878302102" "Defeat all ghosts in area"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P4197375960" "I need you to take care of that rupture over at Jamison."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// LocationName :
"P400873926" "Jamison Office Park"
// EntryString :
"P1647032536" "The ghosts of dimension Alpha Upsilon 24-2 are resentful of their fate. They're more than likely to take out their frustrations on innocent civilians."
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3279127975" "These people will soon know what it is to suffer!"
// Script Variable ACTOR2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P559929936" "To suffer like us!"
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P664430188" "We should have known {HeroName} was to blame!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Ruptures2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2551056331" "You defeated the villains and closed the dimensional rupture."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4201804751" "Thanks for dealing with that dimensional rupture, {HeroName}. I still can hardly believe that villains from all over the multiverse are spilling into Paragon City! We've been treating the symptoms for far too long; we've got to find a way to fight the disease. Somehow, we've got to stop those ruptures from occurring!"
// RandomFameString :
"P3859909578" "Did you hear about those ghosts all over the Jamison Office Park? Thank heaven for {HeroName}!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Errand11 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2950025180" "While you were closing up those dimensional ruptures that opened across the city, Azuria's been preparing the spell that will reunite the Portal scientists whose dimensional fabric was torn in two. She's about ready to fire it up. Maybe, just maybe, we'll learn something from those scientists when she's through. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>In the meantime, I need you to go have another talk with Tina Macintyre.</A> She's been studying the dimensional ruptures non-stop."
// SendOffString :
"P53206434" "Tina's pretty worried about these ruptures."
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3713518834" "Tina's waiting for you, {HeroName}."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4030396854" "Listen, I've been studying what happened to those scientists, and it may be a harbinger of greater dangers to come. I think those scientists were split by a rupture. It opened up right where they were standing, and they were ripped apart at the dimensional seams. I believe that what happened to those scientists could happen to an entire dimension! If these ruptures keep opening in Paragon City, they could wind up tearing our dimension to shreds!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P366127856" "Looks like the rupture situation is getting worse. I've got a number of heroes working on it, but it's all I can do to keep a lid on the situation. If you see any strange baddies around, be sure to give 'em what for. <br><br>On a brighter note, the ritual to reunite the severed scientists was successful. They're back to normal, and talking like human beings again. I have to tell you, the debriefing was a little scary. Just before they got lost, the scientists were hard at work studying the dimensional ruptures. They were beginning to think that the ruptures were caused deliberately. Someone, or something is trying to tear the multiverse apart."
// RandomFameString :
"P132282251" "{HeroName} looks worried about something."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound12 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3283204355" "According to those scientists who got lost in the multiverse, it sounds like these dimensional ruptures might not be accidental. On the contrary, they think that someone is purposely producing the ruptures in an effort to tear whole dimensions apart! The only problem is, we don't know who. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>{HeroName}, I need you to take some readings from the ruptures that have opened up around the multiverse.</A> Can you do it?"
// AcceptString :
"P2155382014" "Take some readings from the ruptures"
// SendOffString :
"P1049412348" "Portal Corporation has located three new ruptures within the multiverse. We've sealed them off in force fields, but you might have to deal with some company."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound12_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3868070215" "Take readings from rupture"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2023323011" "We still don't know who's responsible for causing those ruptures."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3924189068" "It's no surprise that the Freakshow's world is a blasted mess."
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3889012580" "Destructivator"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2250536289" "No one better step on my turf."
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P267705910" "I'm the king of the castle!"
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1720363164" "Did you hear something?"
// Script Variable ACTOR2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1266880515" "Nah. Why's that?"
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P539027913" "Hey! You don't belong here!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Rupture1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// InteractBeginString :
"P3104851160" "You begin to scan the dimensional rupture."
// InteractCompleteString :
"P1730592441" "You have scanned the dimensional rupture."
// InteractActionString :
"P2600169574" "Scanning..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2424097503" "You got some readings from the first rupture."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound12_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2522877278" "We need more data, {HeroName}. Get on it."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3288838209" "It's always a little disturbing to set foot on the streets of the Council Empire."
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P2338747290" "Archon Klein"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3855931986" "See that our security is doubled."
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P1114208506" "I have heard of your skill in battle. Care to prove it?"
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2918608612" "There's a Portal Corporation hero on the premises."
// Script Variable ACTOR2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3651582505" "From that strange, democratic dimension? Again?"
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P186642816" "Surrender at once!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Rupture2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound12_Part3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P1367026011" "A broken beaker bears the logo of a company called Crey Conglomerate."
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P2382333240" "Protector 12173"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P597990233" "A stranger? Here?"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P1145227742" "I want to be alone!"
// Script Variable ACTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1665819904" "I hear..."
// Script Variable ACTOR2_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P326797868" "...a footstep. Someone's here."
// Script Variable ACTOR_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P229634865" "Leave! Leave me!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Rupture3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskBegin 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1687731338" "Portal Corporation cooked up this scanning device. It'll store any relevant data on the ruptures' characteristics."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P295862243" "Good work, {HeroName}. I'll get this data to the lab. Maybe we can figure out who's causing all these dimensional ruptures. Maybe we can even figure out why."
// RandomFameString :
"P3110664782" "Have you seen all those dimensional ruptures around lately?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission13 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1195405461" "The Portal techs had a look at that data you brought us on the dimensional ruptures. Many of them seemed to originate from a particular dimension, Lamda Rho 57-20. Around here, it's better known as Werewolf World. It's a world of perpetual nighttime, which many believe is under the control of Requiem himself. I think Requiem may be responsible for these dimensional ruptures, {HeroName}. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>Will you got to Werewolf World and see if you can track him down?</A> You may have a limited amount of time. Werewolf World has been placed on the restricted list. If you can't get back in 90 minutes, we'll have to pull the plug."
// AcceptString :
"P3254035873" "Go to Werewolf World and track down Requiem"
// SendOffString :
"P1426201436" "I don't know why Requiem would want to destroy other dimensions, but it seems likely that he's behind all this chaos. "
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1102381349" "Seek Requiem"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P821605178" "I need you to track down Requiem."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P1893724133" "The staggering darkness of this world gives you a strangely peaceful feeling."
// Script Variable PATROLLER_ATTACK_DIALOG1 :
"P1942706514" "Graaaahhh!"
// Script Variable PATROLLER_ATTACK_DIALOG2 :
"P3763593588" "Grooooowwwrrr!"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P754586607" "Scar"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2675783673" "Grrrrr."
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P3865482966" "GRRR! GRAAAHH! GRRRAAAHHHH!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Rupture 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P3423292246" "Close the rupture"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P287765978" "You feel a dark presence touch your mind."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskFailure 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2159517285" "So, Requiem is on that world. What's more, he thinks he can hide himself from us. I'm more convinced than ever that he's behind the rash of dimensional ruptures that are threatening to tear apart the multiverse. We need to figure out a way to bring him to light!"
// RandomFameString :
"P1040330533" "I hear strange things are afoot in the multiverse."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnFailure 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound14 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1543704241" "I'm certain that the Requiem of Werewolf World is behind the dimensional ruptures. Why, when he touched your mind, he all but admitted it! If you can defeat him, we may bring a stop to all this chaos. We just need a way to force him to show himself. I want you to go see if Peter Stemitz has some idea of how to do it. Peter's been around a long time, and he knows a great deal about all kinds of monsters."
// AcceptString :
"P3150173183" "Talk to Peter Stemitz"
// SendOffString :
"P634451734" "We're still trying to stay on top of the rupture situation. Watch out for extra-dimensional evil-doers lurking about."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound14_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P4267238848" "Peter's been around the block more times than you might guess. He should be able to help us."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2935142929" "Yo, {HeroName}! How's my favorite hero? You need a way to force Requiem to manifest? Well, I do have an idea. Requiem's not exactly what you'd call a being of pure darkness. The Nictus that fused with his soul is purely dark, but Requiem was originally human. There's a good chance that there's a part of him that still craves the light. I've seen it before. No matter how evil, it's hard for any human to completely turn his back on light forever. So what you need is a pure flame. If I were you, I'd talk to Azuria about that."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound14_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1965819216" "Ask Azuria about pure flame"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3795533651" "Peter's idea is the only one we've got. Go see Azuria about that pure flame."
// Script Variable LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P4066588788" "Has this fool brought us here?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P358053971" "A pure flame? Yes. A clever plan. I myself cannot construct a pure flame; for that you'll need a champion of the people, someone whose inner light is fueled by the love of thousands. Take this candle to Maria Jenkins. In addition to being one of the sweetest women I know, she's earned the respect and love of this city many times over. I believe she'll be able to summon the pure flame."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound14_Part3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P386938325" "Take candle to Maria Jenkins"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P537446902" "This pure flame schtick is the only plan we've got. You best get on it."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1152196162" "Azuria believes I can summon a pure flame? Well, I don't know if I have that kind of power, but I'll try my best. Let me hold the candle. <br><br>Well, I'll be! I should have known better than to doubt Azuria. Is there anything that woman doesn't know?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3750196608" "So, that's pure flame, huh? Pretty beautiful, I guess. Let's just hope it's useful as well. If this will really draw Requiem into the light, we may be able to stop him from tearing the multiverse to shreds!"
// RandomFameString :
"P1280918257" "Did you see {HeroName} carrying around that strange candle? It was beautiful!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission15 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2549767404" "If I understand this pure flame correctly, here's how it works. You carry the flame to Requiem's dimension and make your presence known. Eventually, Requiem will be drawn to the flame. He's been living in darkness for a long time; he won't be able to resist the call of the light. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>Once he shows himself, you've got to defeat Requiem and all of his minions.</A> Maybe that'll put a stop to these dimensional ruptures of his. The trouble is, the technicians have detected some sort of instability in Requiem's dimension. They can only keep a portal there stable for 90 minutes."
// AcceptString :
"P3175402473" "Defeat Requiem and all of his minions"
// SendOffString :
"P3290682428" "Remember, in any dimension, Requiem is a force to be reckoned with."
